  "claimBoundary": "This is a strict source-bound zero-result plan for deciding whether a small external UPS or supercapacitor shutdown reserve is worthwhile for the Raspberry Pi 5 lower-cost reference. D-109 keeps software and storage resilience without required backup power as the incumbent. A vendor specification, UPS topology, capacitor calculation, quoted hold-up time, successful clean shutdown, fewer failures, average, unmeasured cut, one operation, one storage medium, one unit, one temperature, one state of charge, or an aggregate cannot establish sudden-power resilience, committed-state integrity, household safety, degraded-mode availability, lifecycle reliability, complete delivered cost, or net value. A reserve cannot relabel a failed software or storage campaign as qualified. The documented USB 3 SSD lane remains the first storage fallback when qualified microSD misses D-109. Exact final hardware, storage, image, workload, electrical fixture, reserve candidates, revisions, cells, firmware, thresholds, schedule, evidence, results, ranking and authority are open. No purchase, vendor contact, wiring, charging, firmware mutation, destructive electrical operation, target operation, candidate selection, D-109 supersession, BOM mutation, publication or product claim is authorized.",
